Copyright: See inst/COPYRIGHTS and inst/NOTICE for source-level ownership,
    adapted components, and optional linked dependencies.
Description: Native UMAP and interpolation-based t-SNE embeddings, PCA, and
    Louvain and Leiden graph clustering for data matrices or
    precomputed nearest-neighbor graphs. One-call workflows use native CPU
    exact or FAISS HNSW search and Apple Metal exact or IVF-Flat search.
    Optional CUDA support links to the RAPIDS cuVS C API and retains selected
    nearest-neighbor results on the device. Preprocessing, graph or affinity
    construction, fixed-reference transforms, and optimizers report their
    CPU, Metal, or CUDA execution backend. Experimental landmark and
    file-backed routes address larger inputs with method-specific backend
    limits. Selected resident and file-backed CUDA routes coordinate multiple
    GPUs. UMAP exposes neighborhood, metric, graph mode, backend, seed, and
    preprocessing controls; other optimizer settings follow a recorded
    release policy.
